s form part of a danger signal cascade in response to lipopolysaccharide and GroEL</article-title><source>Clin Exp Immunol</source><volume>145</volume><fpage>183</fpage><lpage>189</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16792689</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b6-ehp0115-001573"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dybdahl</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Slordahl</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Waage</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Kierulf</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Espevik</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Sundan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Myocardial ischaemia and the inflammatory response: release of heat shock protein 70 after myocardial infarction</article-title><source>Heart</source><volume>91</volume><fpage>299</fpage><lpage>304</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15710705</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ehp0115-001573"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fenech</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Biomarkers of genetic damage for cancer epidemiology</article-title><source>Toxicology</source><volume>181&#x02013;182</volume><fpage>411</fpage><lpage>416</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp0115-001573"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fenech</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Morley</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1985</year><article-title>Measurement of micronuclei in lymphocytes</article-title><source>Mutat Res</source><volume>147</volume><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3974610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp0115-001573"><citation citation-type="journa